==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 5.33~8 seconds<sup>160f~240f</sup>.
*30 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] spawns as the boss.
**12 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Despite being the first stage, this one is a nasty stage combining elements like a hard-pushing boss, a deadly backliner and a very demanding spam of Wild Doges. The boss, Xenobeast Bunaglios, may seem intimidating, but is set back by his [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] typing, meaning [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] is practically mandatory for this beast.

The support, however, consists of a Master A. with extremely high magnification and the dreaded 200% Wild Doge. Therefore, bringing [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] (and [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer]]) units is strongly recommended. Notably, [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]] is one of the few units with both [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] Traitless and Behemoth Slayer, serving as the perfect counter to Wild Doge while still holding his own against the boss. Additionally, a Level 50 [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] can survive two attacks from a 200% Wild Doge and serve as a supplemental meatshield if needed. Finally, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] can be extremely helpful given their spammability and high DPS.

If you don't have the [[True Form]]s of any [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] from [[Uncanny Legends]], your best bet is stacking [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]] at the beginning of the stage while maxing out your [[Worker Cat]]. Stack at least two Cyberpunks to get both bosses under a perma-Slow. If you let Bunaglios move up even a little, the outer part of Bunaglios' [[Explosion]] will hit your Cyberpunks and either trigger Survive or just kill them.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
''The most reliable options for this stage are in the form of Legend Cat True Forms gated behind [[Atonement for Sin]], which unlocks their Behemoth Slayer abilities. Without them, it is not advised to attempt this stage or subsequent stages. Additionally, you will want all of these units to be at least level 45.''

*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]: A phenomal source of DPS against all enemies in this stage. Behemoth Slayer allows it to withstand several hits from the boss, provided Xenobeast Bunaglios is weakened. Naala's [[Long Distance]] Multi-Hit also enables it to take advantage of peons to deliver devastating damage to the boss from afar.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: A cheap source of [[Surge Attack]] damage against Master A. and Xenobeast Bunaglios. Though unreliable, the damage is absurdly high relative to his cost, making him well worth including. However, Wild Doges remain unaffected, so caution is advised.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]: With [[Resistant]] VS Traitless enemies and Behemoth Slayer, Doguemon can successfully stall out every threat in this stage for some time. While his high price can make him dubious to send out at certain points, he is still effective at stalling Xenobeast Bunaglios for at least a few hits, especially if Bunaglios is [[Weaken]]ed.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat:]] With his Explosion talent and huge burst damage, Awakened Bahamut can be a powerful source of damage against Bunaglios as well as clearing out peons for other units. His piercing attacks can also hit Master A to chip him down. It is recommended to let Awakened Bahamut hit the base to instantly deal 110K damage to Master A/Bunaglios. If you have a [[Talent Orbs|Berserker Orb]] equipped on him, the peons at the start can be used to activate the ability, giving him a damage boost to deal huge starting damage to Bunaglios after spawning.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: An expensive, yet reliable source of Surge Attack damage against Master A. and Xenobeast Bunaglios. His high health allows him to remain on the field longer compared to other Behemoth Slayer units, provided Bunaglios does not [[Critical Hit]].
*[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] / [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: Both of these units are basically required for not only this stage, but all four Xenobeast stages. Cat Egg Pod also has very high damage against Behemoths, so much so that it can even OHKO Wild Doge here, making your life a lot easier.
*[[Courier Cat]]: Possessing crazy stats against Behemoths, Courier is amazing for chipping down the Wild Doges and Xenobeast itself. Courier Cat can survive one of the outer Explosions that Xenobeast generates, which can help a lot when timing it.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: A must-have for this stage, provided with its extreme health and immunities, it can wall off the dangerous threats for a short while. It can also help you protect ground during Soap's downtime, preventing Xenobeast from pushing crazily hard.
*[[Cyberpunk Cat]]: With a guaranteed Slow effect against every single enemy here, Cyberpunk is invaluable in controlling the enemies. It can also deal chip damage to the Master A. and Xenobeast.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]]: Despite Xenobeast having a chance to Critical Hit just to counter Metal Cat, it is still amazing for the stage thanks to how the chance isn't guaranteed, and Metal Cat can help protect precious ground when there aren't any Soap Cats or Cat Egg Pods around. Keep in mind how the Squire Rels can melt through it.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
''Xenobeast Bunaglios has an incredibly high forward piercing range through his [[Explosion]] ability, meaning any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that outranges his 675 effective range is suitable for this stage.

*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]]/[[Moonshade Kaworu (Legend Rare Cat)|Moonshade Kaworu]]: Their Long Distance Multi-Hit lets them snipe Master A. even if Xenobeast Bunaglios is blocking their way. For Izanami, scoring a [[Savage Blow]] or two on him is invaluable, and makes the rest of the fight significantly easier when she inevitably dies. Kaworu survives a bit longer thanks to his Immunity to Explosions.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]]: All the enemies are within Lunos' target traits, and combined with his Explosions Immunity, he can make this stage trivial. His Conjure Spirit not only funds his deploy cost, but can also boost your team's finance. Combined with his extremely fast cooldown of 10 seconds, you will never lose this stage with him.
*[[Supernova Cosmo]]: He comfortably outranges Xenobeast and his Explosions, allowing him to fire off his devastating nukes every once in a while. His waves also one-shot the peons here while chipping down the boss and Master A.

